== refusal
Ovenlight won't change this policy on its own:
  - nodeAttrs entry 1 gives ["funnel"] to "*", which may include guest devices; change its target to autogroup:member, or the users, groups and tags that need it
  - nodeAttrs entry 3 gives ["drive:share"] to "autogroup:tagged", "tailnet-half", which may include guest devices; change its target to autogroup:member, or the users, groups and tags that need it
  - autoApprovers.routes["10.0.0.0/24"] lists "tag:ovenlight-guest-coach", which may include guest devices, so a guest device could have what it advertises (routes, an exit node) approved automatically and carry your traffic; list only the users, groups or tags of your own devices there
  - autoApprovers.routes["192.168.0.0/16"] lists "autogroup:future", which may include guest devices, so a guest device could have what it advertises (routes, an exit node) approved automatically and carry your traffic; list only the users, groups or tags of your own devices there
  - autoApprovers.exitNode lists "autogroup:danger-all", which may include guest devices, so a guest device could have what it advertises (routes, an exit node) approved automatically and carry your traffic; list only the users, groups or tags of your own devices there
  - autoApprovers.services["svc:web"] lists "*", which may include guest devices, so a guest device could have what it advertises (routes, an exit node) approved automatically and carry your traffic; list only the users, groups or tags of your own devices there

Suggested manual edit:
  Make the changes above in the admin console (Access controls).
  Then run the same ovenlight command again.
